# `.claude/` is deliberately TRACKED, not ignored.
#
# This repo publishes its own governance: the rules files, the hook scripts and
# the skills under `.claude/` are the enforcement layer for the read-only rule
# and the publishing rule, and a reader who cannot see them cannot audit them.
# Ignoring the directory would also make the choice by accident on the first
# `git add -A`, which is the outcome this file exists to prevent.
#
# The exception is anything holding private match patterns. The publishing rule
# bars the maintainer's own name and this estate's hostnames from the repo, and
# the leak-detection hook matches on exactly those — so its pattern list cannot
# live in a published file. `.claude/private-patterns.example` is committed and
# shows the format; the real list is local-only, by construction.
.claude/*.local
.claude/settings.local.json

# A report is nothing but hostnames, serials and MACs, and the README tells you
# to generate one with `> "$(hostname)-$(date +%F).md"`. Run that in a clone and
# `git add -A` publishes the estate. Root level only — docs/ is dated prose.
/*-20??-??-??.md
